## Copilot-Specific Capabilities

- Select `sdlc-supervisor` in Copilot Chat or invoke it as `@sdlc-supervisor`.
- The Supervisor can delegate to the PM, Designer, Architect, Developer,
  Reviewer, and QA custom agents through native subagent support.
- VS Code can provide interactive file-approval and terminal-confirmation UX.
- Prompt files such as `/start-new-feature` and `/fix-failing-tests` provide
  repeatable entry points.

These capabilities improve interaction but do not replace the portable scripts,
tracked spec, task graph, permission rules, or evidence records.

## Project Configuration

Read `.github/sdlc-config.yml` before work. It is the source of truth for the
stack, package manager, test directories, named validation tasks, security
policy, and optional readiness controls. Run
`scripts/validate-sdlc-config.ps1` or `.sh` after configuring it.

## Worker Expectations

- Keep application code in `src/` and tests in `tests/` unless the selected
  project contract says otherwise.
- Make small, focused changes and preserve existing project conventions.
- Never hardcode secrets, keys, or tokens.
- The Developer verifies a clean build before review.
- The Reviewer runs the scope audit and reports findings without changing the
  workflow state.
- QA runs configured tests and reports failures verbatim.

The Supervisor is the only agent that records final transitions, gate metadata,
review-cycle changes, and terminal completion.